  "description": "Health of the LGTM stack itself, built ENTIRELY from series already scraped by the collector's prometheus/internal jobs (Tempo + Mimir + collector /metrics, filtered to the incident-relevant families). These same series drive the stack-alerts.yaml rules; this dashboard makes them visible DURING an incident instead of alert-only. Zero new ingest. READ THE ROWS TOP TO BOTTOM AS ONE PATH: producer -> collector receiver -> collector exporter -> backend. The 'Collector ingest' row covers the first two hops; the 'Silent-failure signals' row covers the backend hop. A drop is only ruled out when both read clean, because refused==0 says nothing about a backend that accepts a write and then discards it.",
