    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Mimir-Prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Loki discards log entries PER ENTRY: an oversized entry is dropped and counted here, the rest of the push is ingested, and the whole request still answers 400. That partial-success shape lets a discard run unnoticed for a long time - the service keeps logging while a large share of its entries are dropped. Unscoped by reason on purpose: scoping to the one reason seen so far is how the next reason arrives silently. A HEALTHY 0 MUST STILL BE VISIBLE, so axisSoftMin is negative - with min:0 a series at exactly 0 draws on the axis floor, is clipped, and the panel reads as EMPTY, which is indistinguishable from no-data. Alert: LokiSamplesDiscarded (warning, 15m). Relayed via the loki-internal self-scrape keep-list plus the filter/internal_metrics allowlist in config/otel-collector-config.yaml; a name missing from either one keeps NOTHING and this panel goes silently blank.\nThis panel is EMPTY on a healthy box, not a zero line. Loki creates each loki_discarded_* series per REASON on the first discard, so 'no series' means 'nothing has ever been discarded' - the good state, and why LokiSamplesDiscarded rather than this panel is what catches the transition. Do not read an empty panel here as a broken relay: cross-check the ruler panels beside it, which are never empty on a live stack.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisSoftMin": -0.05,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 38
      },
      "id": 12,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
