      "description": "The Loki ruler's own remote_write queue to Mimir (config/loki-config.yaml, ruler.remote_write). Read the three series TOGETHER - that is the whole point of relaying all three rather than just the failure counter:\n  appended  - the ruler EVALUATED a rule and wrote a sample to its WAL. Flat at zero means the ruler stopped evaluating, OR Loki is receiving no logs at all (the heartbeat rule is sum(count_over_time(...[5m])), and sum() over no lines returns an EMPTY vector, so a quiet stack legitimately appends nothing).\n  sent      - samples handed to the remote-write queue. Tracking appended = healthy.\n  failed    - NON-RECOVERABLE sends. Recoverable ones are retried, so every increment here is a recorded sample that is permanently lost.\nAlerts: LokiRulerRemoteWriteFailing (ratio, 15m) and LokiRulerNotAppending (absent-guarded, 30m). Note appended is per-tenant while sent/failed carry remote_name and url, so they are summed here rather than grouped.",
